.TH SPARKLINK.CONF 5 "2025-04-05" "SparkLink" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
sparklink.conf \- SparkLink daemon configuration file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/sparklink/main.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
This file controls the runtime behaviour of
.BR slkd (8).
It uses TOML syntax.
.PP
If the file does not exist or cannot be parsed, the daemon starts with
built\-in defaults.
.SH SECTIONS
.SS [general]
.TP
.B discovery_level
Integer 0\(en4. Minimum discovery level filter for scan results.
Devices advertising below this level are ignored. Default:
.BR 1 .
.TP
.B auto_enable
Boolean. Automatically power on the adapter at daemon startup. Default:
.BR true .
.TP
.B name
String. Local device name advertised to peers. Default:
.BR \(dqSparkLink\(dq .
.SS [policy]
.TP
.B auto_pair
Boolean. Automatically accept pairing requests. Default:
.BR false .
.TP
.B min_encryption
Integer 0\(en3. Minimum encryption level required for incoming connections.
.B 0
disables enforcement. Default:
.BR 0 .
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
[general]
discovery_level = 1
auto_enable = true
name = "Living Room Hub"

[policy]
auto_pair = false
min_encryption = 0
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/sparklink/main.conf
Default location loaded by
.BR slkd (8).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR slkd (8),
.BR slctl (1)
